+# PHASE 1 protocol — confirm the adopted rules and compare the evaluations
+
+Status: **proposed, awaiting supervisor approval and the reviewed M1 throughput pilot.**
+No game has been played under this protocol. Human study remains pending.
+
+This protocol is the frozen plan for the measurement part of `campaign/campaign-contract.md`
+§ "Phase 1". It uses only existing seams: `RunSpec`, the `asymmetric` `fen`/`fenSwapped` pair,
+`buildJobs`, `evalParams`, `run`, and the existing analysers. It adds no framework and changes no
+gameplay default, weight or dependency.
+
+Revision 2026-09-22: corrected after supervisor review — finite per-move time guards, time-based
+(not depth-based) primary comparison, a physical-game ledger, censoring-aware cap analysis, honest
+independent-unit accounting, and removal of the `--depth` shortcut and the unsupported
+depth-proxy/equivalent claims.
+
+## 0. Authorization boundary
+
+- Allowed: prepare specs/setups, parse and validate them, run the M1 throughput probes after
+  review, then the campaign batches after review.
+- Not allowed here: playing campaign games, training or replacing weights, changing defaults,
+  adopting or reverting a rule, or claiming a capped game as a completed ending.
+- The three integrity fixes named in the contract (LAN replay, source identity, condition
+  statistics) are prerequisites owned by other workstreams and are not part of this package.
+
+## 1. Frozen rules under test
+
+Every arm freezes the same current adopted rule set, written explicitly in `rules` so a later
+default change cannot alter a run:
+
+| field | frozen value |
+|---|---|
+| `archerShots` | `plusDiagFwd2` (the adopted +2 **forward** diagonals on top of classic) |
+| `archerMove` | `any` |
+| `archerChecks` | `true` |
+| `beastMove` | `any` |
+| `beastCapture` | `adjacent` (all eight neighbours; capture is separate from the step) |
+| `beastCaptureForward` | `true` (the forward blind spot is removed) |
+| `beastChains` | `true` |
+| `guardImmune` | `true`, `guardCaptures: none`, `guardStep: 1` |
+| `promotionSet` | `standard` (ordinary chess promotions) |
+| `paladinKamikaze` | `nonPawn` |
+| `bishopsOppositeColours` | `true` |
+| `fiftyMove`, `threefold`, `insufficientMaterial` | `true` |
+
+Engine values stay the shipped constants (`--values` unset); both archer arms use the same values,
+so the classic-arm comparison is not re-priced. This is a stated limitation, not a hidden one.
+
+## 2. Setups
+
+`campaign/setups/phase-1.json` holds **96 explicit legal full-board setups** with stable IDs
+`P1-001`…`P1-096`: 64 mirror starts (`P1-001`…`P1-064`) and 32 asymmetric starts
+(`P1-065`…`P1-096`). Generation is deterministic and reconstructible with
+`campaign/setups/phase-1-generate.ts` (`mulberry32(20260922)`, distinct ranks from the project
+`POOL = QLRRBBNNAAGMMSS`, sampled by `sampleBackRank` so the bishop-colour rule holds).
+
+Coverage: 71 distinct White compositions; White letter counts Q/R/L/B/N/A/G/M/S =
+46/104/37/78/93/83/46/89/96; Black = 49/98/35/78/98/80/49/87/98; 61 setups with an Archer in both
+armies; 73 with a Beast in both; 54 with a Guard on one side.
+
+### 2.1 Pair, colour and modulo mapping
+
+`buildJobs` (`pairs: true`) sets `config = asymmetric[pairId % N]`, where `N` is the number of
+listed setups and `pairId = k` for pair `k`. So **pair `k` uses setup `k mod N`**, and the list
+repeats when `games/2 > N`. Game `2k` uses that setup's `fen` with the spec's white AI config on
+White; game `2k+1` uses its `fenSwapped` with the same config on Black. `fenSwapped` is the
+colour-and-rank mirror (rank `r → 7-r`, case swapped, White to move); a mirror start is
+self-mirroring, an asymmetric start maps to the other army.
+
+`commonSeeds` gives every pair in a stream the same opening RNG stream, but it does **not** guarantee
+identical played openings: a rule that changes the legal-move set (for example `archerShots`) can
+make the random opening choose different moves. Claim equal seeds, not equal positions.
+
+### 2.2 Independent units and structural duplicates
+
+An independent unit is `(setup, opening stream, orientation)`. For a **single-engine** arm (same
+settings on both sides), the two orientations of a **mirror** start have the same seed, the same
+start position and the same engine, so they are structurally the same game (they may still diverge
+because a time-limited search is not deterministic). They must not be counted as two independent
+observations. `campaign/verify-phase-1.ts` reports, per spec, `physical`, `independentUnits` and
+`structuralDuplicates`; for example the 400-game archer pilot is 254 independent units
+(146 structural duplicates) and the 1600-game evaluator match is 1600 independent units
+(no duplicates, because the evaluations swap sides).
+
+The validator proves, with no game played: canonical FEN round-trip, one king per side, no pawn on a
+back rank, no lab piece (`O/C/V/T`), status `playing`, at least one legal move, `fenSwapped` equals
+the independent mirror, the modulo pair mapping, and that every job FEN is a frozen setup FEN.
+
+## 3. Arms and search budget
+
+Every run is **time-based with an explicit finite `timeMs` per move** and **no depth cap**, so
+`sideOptions` never returns `timeMs = Infinity`. The primary comparison uses **equal practical
+per-move time** on both sides, not equal advertised depth. The confirmed per-move time is selected
+by the M1 throughput pilot (gate T1); `100 ms` in the JSON is a provisional placeholder.
+
+- **Archer A/B (two populations).** `phase-1-archer-adopted` (`plusDiagFwd2`) and
+  `phase-1-archer-classic` (`classic`); one rule differs. 61 setups with an Archer in both armies,
+  seed 8101.
+- **Evaluator primary (head-to-head, one run).** `phase-1-eval-linear-vs-residual`: White
+  `sim/nnue/eval-linear.json`, Black `campaign/specs/phase-1-residual-eval.json`, `pairs: true`
+  swaps the sides each game. All 96 setups, seed 8102. Equal finite per-move time both sides, no
+  depth cap. Both sides use `evalParams`, so the per-ply evaluation-swap and transposition-drop
+  overhead is identical; reached depth and actual nodes/ms are recorded per move.
+- **Evaluator sensitivity (one run).** `phase-1-eval-linear-extra-time`: the linear side gets 4×
+  the per-move time of residual (400 ms vs 100 ms), both finite, no depth cap. This is a
+  **sensitivity arm**, not a mechanism proof.
+- **Beast/Guard focus (descriptive).** `phase-1-beast-guard-focus`: 73 Beast-both setups, seed
+  8104.
+- **Throughput probes.** `phase-1-throughput-t50/t100/t200`: 24 games each, 12 setups, seeds
+  8155/8205/8305, no depth cap.
+
+The residual arm is the campaign-owned pinned file. It embeds the exact bytes of the adopted blob
+from `src/ai/nnue/weights.ts` in the existing `EvalParams` format
+(`evaluator: "residual"`, `net: { b64, kind: "residual" }`).
+
+## 4. Residual path — what is proven
+
+`campaign/verify-phase-1.ts` proves from the executable path, with no game played:
+
+- `src/ai/nnue/weights.ts` loads a real net: `netLoaded = true`, `netKind() = 'residual'`, base64
+  length 120408, and
+  `sha256(base64) = e17a27bfbadb029e419082ce8dae4b3c6df7ca6e4d983e02b975772f60c9b58c`, matching the
+  accepted Q6 model sha in `docs/research/ai-q6-acceptance-2026-09-16.md`.
+- The simulation worker's default evaluator is `linear`; `evalParams` is the switch; the pinned arm
+  loads as `residual`.
+- On the 96 current-game setups the residual changes the static evaluation on 94 of 96 positions
+  (`mean |Δ| = 21.10 cp`, `max |Δ| = 50 cp`, no value over the ±150 clip).
+- A position with an Ogre falls back to linear (`Δ = 0`); this lab fallback is **not** residual
+  evidence.
+
+Recorded divergence (informational): `sim/nnue/net.json` re-quantises to a different blob than the
+committed one, so `gen.ts arms` would pin the wrong net; do not regenerate the arm files from it.
+The repository file `sim/nnue/eval-residual.json` has no `net` field; the campaign pinned arm
+supplies it.
+
+## 5. Hypotheses and endpoints
+
+### H1 — evaluator
+
+The adopted residual evaluation is at least 20 Elo stronger than the linear evaluation at the same
+practical per-move time budget.
+
+- **P1 (primary):** in `phase-1-eval-linear-vs-residual`, the residual-side score over
+  colour-swapped pairs, reported as Elo(residual − linear) on **all records** and on complete pairs.
+- **P1b (sensitivity):** in `phase-1-eval-linear-extra-time`, the residual-side score when linear
+  gets 4× the time. A residual loss here is **sensitivity evidence** that the advantage may be
+  bought with search cost; it is **not** proof that residual is "only a depth proxy".
+- **SWE:** 20 Elo (≈ 0.0287 score) for both.
+- Decision (prespecified): keep the current default (residual) unless the setup-clustered 95% CI
+  for P1 lies entirely below +20 Elo. If the CI is wide or includes 0, keep the current default
+  unchanged and report a bounded inconclusive result. **No equivalence, adoption or reversion is
+  declared.**
+
+### H2 — adopted Archer
+
+- **P2a (primary):** decisive-share difference (adopted − classic), with a censoring-aware treatment
+  of caps (§7). **SWE: +3.0 percentage points** in favour of the adopted arm.
+- **P2b (fairness):** paired White-score difference, SWE 0.02, plus the absolute balance gate
+  `|White score − 0.5| ≤ 0.03` on complete pairs and a conservative bound that accounts for caps.
+- **P3 (secondary):** draw rate, cap count, mean plies, Archer shots and Beast chains per game,
+  promotions per game, actual cost (`ms`, `nodes`) per side.
+- Decision: if P2a and P2b are near equal (inside the SWE) or the sample is underpowered, keep the
+  current rule unchanged (per `LESSONS.md`).
+
+### H3 — Beast/Guard review (descriptive)
+
+No confirmatory test. Select the longest Beast chains, the clearest blocked-Guard structures and the
+longest full endings from the pilot records and report their counts.
+
+## 6. Uncertainty — paired, setup-clustered
+
+- Common requirements: report raw counts, the number of independent setups, complete pairs and
+  incomplete pairs.
+- Target estimator (both contrasts): cluster by setup (`configId`). Per setup compute the paired
+  statistic, then a cluster bootstrap over setups (10,000 resamples, percentile 95% CI).
+
+**Required analysis that is absent** (state it, do not assume it exists):
+
+1. A head-to-head per-side-`evalParams` report. `src/sim/experiments.ts` has no path that folds a
+   mixed linear-vs-residual match to one side.
+2. Censoring-aware cap bounds (§7). No estimator handles `plyCap` as censoring.
+3. The setup-clustered bootstrap. It is not in `src/sim/analyze.ts`.
+4. A matched-start/provenance audit. The `runAb` paired interval is over `byConfig` keys for two
+   same-rule populations; **seed equality is not position matching**, and `runAb` does not verify
+   `startFen` parity or source/spec identity between arms.
+5. Game-record unit de-duplication. Only the static structural analysis in the verifier exists.
+6. Per-evaluator cost aggregation and an endgame-tail selector.
+7. A Guard-block counter (`Events` has no `guardBlocks` field).
+
+Until these exist, P1/P2 are read from a sensitivity table, not from a finished confirmatory
+analysis.
+
+## 7. Caps versus endings (informative censoring)
+
+- Every phase-1 spec sets `adjudicate: false`. Only true endings (checkmate, stalemate, `draw50`,
+  `drawRepetition`, `drawMaterial`) and `plyCap` occur.
+- A `plyCap` record is **not** a completed ending. Prespecify and report the all-record cap count
+  per run.
+- Conservative bounds (report alongside any ended-only number):
+  - Score: lower bound counts every cap as a loss for the arm under test; upper bound counts every
+    cap as a win. An ended-only score is **conditional** and is labelled as such.
+  - Decisive share: report the ended-only share (caps removed from numerator and denominator) and a
+    conservative bound that counts every cap as non-decisive.
+  - Fairness: report the White-score bounds under both cap assignments.
+- Paired observations: if either game of a pair caps or is missing, the pair is **incomplete**. Do
+  not synthesize a draw or an intact pair. Report the incomplete-pair count; use game-level
+  conservative bounds, or restrict a paired estimate to complete pairs and label it conditional.
+- If the cap share at the confirmed time exceeds 20% in either arm, stop and escalate.
+
+## 8. Design, budget ledger and stopping rules
+
+Two-stage: a pilot per run, then an in-place expansion to the ledger cap (`--games`, same run id,
+same `specKey`; `buildJobs` is a prefix so the pilot games are not replayed). Confirmation uses
+separate run ids with unseen seeds and is a fixed, independent sample.
+
+Physical GameRecords are counted **once**. An N-game head-to-head match is N records; each
+evaluation participates in all N. The ledger is `campaign/specs/phase-1-budget-ledger.json`.
+
+| run id | kind | JSON games | pilot | cap | confirmation |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `phase-1-throughput-t50` | probe | 24 | 24 | 24 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-throughput-t100` | probe | 24 | 24 | 24 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-throughput-t200` | probe | 24 | 24 | 24 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-archer-adopted` | rule population | 400 | 400 | 1600 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-archer-classic` | rule population | 400 | 400 | 1600 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-eval-linear-vs-residual` | evaluator head-to-head | 400 | 400 | 1600 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-eval-linear-extra-time` | evaluator sensitivity | 400 | 400 | 800 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-beast-guard-focus` | descriptive | 200 | 200 | 400 | 0 |
+| `phase-1-archer-adopted-confirm` | confirmation | 800 | 0 | 800 | 800 |
+| `phase-1-archer-classic-confirm` | confirmation | 800 | 0 | 800 | 800 |
+| `phase-1-eval-linear-vs-residual-confirm` | confirmation | 800 | 0 | 800 | 800 |
+
+Totals: throughput probes 72 · pilots 1,800 (1,872 with probes) · expansion additions 4,200 ·
+fixed confirmation 2,400 · **planned 8,472** · phase cap 10,000 · **reserve 1,528 (unspent)**.
+Reserve is a ceiling, not a target, and is not spent for being available.
+
+Stopping and expansion rules:
+
+1. Run the throughput probes (gate T1) and select the confirmed per-move time `T*`.
+2. Freeze reviewed JSON copies at `T*` (see §9) before any main run; then run the pilots.
+3. Expand each main run to its ledger cap unconditionally for the key contrasts (archer and
+   evaluator primary). If a pilot is clearly underpowered, stop that contrast and report a bounded
+   inconclusive result; pooled pilot+expansion intervals are then **descriptive only**.
+4. Confirmation runs (unseen seeds) are the only fixed independent confirmatory sample; decisions
+   rest on them, not on pooled data.
+5. Extensions count cumulatively against 10,000. A larger expansion needs a new supervisor review.
+
+## 9. Exact command plan (after approval; nothing here has been run)
+
+There is **no `--depth` shortcut**: `--depth` sets only `spec.ai.depth`, which per-side `ai.white`
+and `ai.black` objects ignore, so it cannot select the confirmed setting. Freeze reviewed JSON
+copies first: set the confirmed `timeMs` in the proposed files, re-run `campaign/verify-phase-1.ts`,
+and commit the frozen copies before launch. No source or spec change may follow an active run
+(`checkResume` enforces its identity).
+
+```sh
+# Gate T1: throughput probes (supervisor reviews and selects T*)
+node_modules/.bin/tsx src/sim/run.ts --spec campaign/specs/phase-1-throughput-t50.proposed.json --workers 2
+node_modules/.bin/tsx src/sim/run.ts --spec campaign/specs/phase-1-throughput-t100.proposed.json --workers 2
+node_modules/.bin/tsx src/sim/run.ts --spec campaign/specs/phase-1-throughput-t200.proposed.json --workers 2
+
+# Pilots (frozen copies at T*)
+node_modules/.bin/tsx src/sim/run.ts --spec campaign/specs/phase-1-archer-adopted.proposed.json --workers 2
+node_modules/.bin/tsx src/sim/run.ts --spec campaign/specs/phase-1-archer-classic.proposed.json --workers 2
